module gunbc.stage0_emit_plan_generated

// THIS PROJECTION HAS NO PRODUCER, and the note below asserted one until 2026-08-20. Its named
// authority `gunbc.stage0_emit_plan` is DELETED -- `gunbc.generated_projection_paths` records the
// deletion in its own header ("One source remains after the stage0_emit_plan deletion") -- and
// `gunbc.roster_registry` still registers this roster `ByDerivation` from that dead module. So
// "regenerate via generated_artifact_gate main_wet" is false: main_wet leaves this file untouched,
// which is why two rows here survived the disappearance of the thing they describe.
//
// THE TWO ROWS REMOVED. `gunbc_namespace_reference_derived_closure_{admission,contract}.rs` were
// listed here as generated stage0 files and declared in the seed's lib.rs, but their `.dag`
// authorities under dag/gunbc are no longer reachable from the src/v1 import closure, so the emit
// has not produced them for some time and no Rust in the crate referenced them. They were the last
// two names in `--required-regen`'s population refusal. The removal is verified rather than
// asserted: with the two files deleted, the emitted lib.rs and the committed lib.rs differ by
// exactly the two `pub mod` lines this change also deletes and by nothing else (measured, remote
// runner, this branch) -- so the committed seed converges ONTO its authority's output here.
//
// EDITING A GENERATED FILE BY HAND IS NORMALLY THE ONE UNHEALABLE DRIFT CLASS, and this is stated
// rather than quietly done: with the generator deleted, this file is de facto hand-maintained and
// has been since that deletion. The honest repair is to restore a producer or to reclassify the
// roster, and neither is this change's subject; what this change refuses to do is leave a roster
// naming files that do not exist so that regen keeps refusing.
data stage0_emit_plan_generated_note: String = "Projection of the stage0 emit plan. ITS PRODUCER gunbc.stage0_emit_plan IS DELETED, so it is hand-maintained in fact (see the block above); main_wet does not rewrite it. DECLARED SCAFFOLD supply; dissolve-on: generated_artifact_gate accepts v2.compiler.source_authority.ModuleStorageIndex, then the host supply deletes. Regen via dag/tools/generated_artifact_gate.dag main_wet."

